# --- chat ---
etobackup.msg.not_running=Backups are not running here: the repository could not be opened.
etobackup.msg.busy=A backup task is running, try again shortly.
etobackup.msg.failed=Failed: %s
etobackup.msg.backup_failed=Backup failed: %s
etobackup.msg.no_permission=You need OP level 2 for this.
etobackup.msg.taking=Taking a snapshot.
etobackup.msg.made=Snapshot of %s taken: %s files, %s; %s added to the repository.
etobackup.msg.row.auto=%s  automatic, +%s
etobackup.msg.row.manual=%s  on request, +%s
etobackup.msg.row.prerollback=%s  before a rollback, +%s
etobackup.msg.total=%s snapshots, the newest last. Click one to put its rollback command into the chat box.
etobackup.msg.already=A rollback is already under way.
etobackup.msg.no_snapshot=There is no snapshot %s.
etobackup.msg.no_world=The snapshot of %s has no world files.
etobackup.msg.damaged=The snapshot of %s cannot be used: %s of its parts are damaged or missing. Nothing was changed.
etobackup.msg.countdown=%s is putting the world back to the snapshot of %s. Everything since then will be undone; the server restarts in %s seconds.
etobackup.msg.countdown_world=%s is putting the world back to the snapshot of %s. Everything since then will be undone; the world closes in %s seconds and opens again.
etobackup.msg.cancel=[Cancel]
etobackup.msg.cancelled=%s cancelled the rollback.
etobackup.msg.nothing_to_cancel=There is no rollback to cancel.
etobackup.msg.nothing_to_undo=There is no rollback to undo.
etobackup.msg.aborted=The rollback was called off, the world is unchanged: %s
etobackup.msg.done=%s put the world back to the snapshot of %s. /etobackup undo returns to the world before that.
etobackup.msg.not_done=The rollback by %s to the snapshot of %s did not happen, the world is unchanged: %s
etobackup.msg.problem=%s
etobackup.msg.verified=Snapshot %s: %s objects, %s, %s damaged or missing.
etobackup.msg.restored=Restored the snapshot of %s (%s files, %s) into %s
etobackup.msg.reloaded=Reloaded config/etobackup.cfg.
etobackup.msg.reloaded_directory=Reloaded config/etobackup.cfg. The new repository directory takes effect when the server or world starts next time.
etobackup.kick.now=%s is putting the world back to how it was less than a minute ago. The server is restarting; join again in about a minute.
etobackup.kick.minute=%s is putting the world back to how it was a minute ago. The server is restarting; join again in about a minute.
etobackup.kick.minutes=%s is putting the world back to how it was %s minutes ago. The server is restarting; join again in about a minute.
etobackup.kick.hours=%s is putting the world back to how it was %s hours ago. The server is restarting; join again in about a minute.
etobackup.kick.days=%s is putting the world back to how it was %s days ago. The server is restarting; join again in about a minute.

